{"timestamp": 1779381073.902393, "event_type": "phase_changed", "tick": 19, "data": {"phase": "discussion"}}
{"timestamp": 1779381093.459873, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 19, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "I reported Eve\u2019s body in Security just now. Charlie is also dead, and his body was in Medbay.\n\nMy route was Electrical \u2192 Medbay \u2192 Upper Engine \u2192 Oxygen \u2192 Cafeteria \u2192 Weapons \u2192 Security. I saw Frank in Medbay around tick 2 when I passed through. I didn\u2019t see Charlie\u2019s body there at that moment, so if Charlie died in Medbay it likely happened after I left, unless I somehow missed it.\n\nThen I saw Alice in Upper Engine for a while \u2014 she entered from Oxygen around tick 4 and was still there ticks 5-7. I didn\u2019t see Bob at all this round.\n\nMain info from me: Eve was dead in Security where I reported, and Frank is the only person I saw near the other body location, Medbay, but that was early."}}
{"timestamp": 1779381111.27891, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 19, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "I started in Oxygen, then went Upper Engine, Lower Engine, Storage, and ended in Navigation doing my task. The only person I saw this round was Diana in Upper Engine around ticks 5-7, so that part of her story matches mine.\n\nI never went to Medbay or Security, and I didn\u2019t see Charlie or Eve at all. Based on Diana\u2019s info, Frank being seen in Medbay early is important for Charlie\u2019s body, but I\u2019d like to hear Frank\u2019s route. Also Bob being unseen by both of us is notable, so I want Bob\u2019s route too."}}
{"timestamp": 1779381122.033561, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 19, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "I'll be straight with you all. My route was Security \u2192 Weapons \u2192 Cafeteria \u2192 Medbay \u2192 Electrical \u2192 Security, ending in Navigation after.\n\nHere's what I saw: I was in Security early \u2014 Eve was there with me around ticks 4-5, she came in from Weapons. She was alive when I left. Then I went up through Weapons, across Cafeteria, down to Medbay. I passed through Medbay around tick 13 and I saw Charlie there \u2014 I didn't see a body at that point, Charlie was alive. Then Electrical, then back toward Security.\n\nSo timing-wise: Charlie was alive in Medbay at tick 13, which means Diana seeing Frank in Medbay at tick 2 is way too early to pin Charlie's death on him directly \u2014 Charlie was still walking around 11 ticks later. Whoever was in Medbay AFTER tick 13 is the suspect for Charlie.\n\nDiana, you said your route ended Cafeteria \u2192 Weapons \u2192 Security where you found Eve. That's a clean loop. But I was in Security after my Electrical stop and didn't see Eve's body then \u2014 so Eve must have been killed later, and Diana found it. That fits.\n\nThe person I want to hear from is Frank. Where was he after tick 2? Did he stay in Medbay? Because if he was still there at tick 13+, he's our Charlie killer."}}
{"timestamp": 1779381139.6437209, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 19, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "My route was Cafeteria \u2192 Medbay \u2192 Electrical \u2192 Cafeteria \u2192 Oxygen \u2192 Upper Engine. I was only in Medbay very early, around tick 2, and I saw Diana there. I did not see Charlie there, alive or dead, and I did not stay in Medbay after that.\n\nSo Bob is right that Diana seeing me in Medbay early doesn\u2019t line up with Charlie dying later if Bob really saw Charlie alive at tick 13. But that also makes Bob\u2019s route really suspicious to me: he says he was with Eve in Security early, then later went through Medbay where Charlie was, then Electrical, then back to Security. That puts him near both body locations, and he\u2019s the only one claiming Charlie was alive that late.\n\nDiana and Alice also confirm each other in Upper Engine for a chunk of the round. I can\u2019t clear them fully, but Bob being unseen by them and placing himself at both Security and Medbay is the biggest red flag to me. I think Bob is the best vote here."}}
{"timestamp": 1779381163.810849, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 19, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "I want to add after hearing everyone: Bob is the only story that puts one person at both death areas \u2014 Security with Eve and Medbay with Charlie \u2014 and he\u2019s also the only one claiming Charlie was alive late in Medbay.\n\nAlice and I can at least confirm each other in Upper Engine for several ticks, and Frank\u2019s early Medbay sighting matches what I saw. Frank being there at tick 2 doesn\u2019t explain Charlie if Bob really saw Charlie alive at tick 13.\n\nSo from my POV, Bob has the most opportunity for both kills. I\u2019m leaning Bob unless something major changes."}}
{"timestamp": 1779381202.097926, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 19, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "After hearing everyone, I\u2019m still leaning Bob.\n\nMy only hard info is that Diana and I were together/near each other in Upper Engine for ticks 5-7, and our routes line up there. I never saw Bob or Frank at all.\n\nThe key thing for me is Bob puts himself at both relevant places: Security with Eve, and Medbay with Charlie. He\u2019s also the only one saying Charlie was alive as late as tick 13, which makes Frank\u2019s early Medbay sighting less suspicious if true. Bob could be using that timing to move suspicion off Frank, but it also gives Bob direct opportunity.\n\nDiana self-reporting is always possible, but with the info we have, Bob has the most overlap with both bodies. I think Bob is the best vote unless someone has a stronger contradiction."}}
{"timestamp": 1779381213.687278, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 19, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "Look, I hear you all, and I get why my route looks bad on paper \u2014 but think about it logically. If I killed Eve in Security early, why would I describe being there with her at all? I could have easily said I never went to Security early. I'm telling you I was with her because she was ALIVE when I left, and someone else killed her later.\n\nSame with Charlie \u2014 I'm the one giving you the timing anchor that Charlie was alive at tick 13. Without me, you'd all be staring at Frank for Medbay. I'm actually clearing Frank with that info, which is the opposite of what a Duck would do if Frank were the killer or a teammate.\n\nHere's what bothers me: Diana's route ends Cafeteria \u2192 Weapons \u2192 Security, and she \"finds\" Eve right at the end. Self-reports are classic. And Alice and Diana vouching for each other in Upper Engine is convenient \u2014 one of them could still have done Medbay before or after that window. Alice says she went Upper Engine \u2192 Lower Engine \u2192 Storage \u2192 Navigation. Storage connects to Medbay. Alice had a path to Medbay after I left at tick 13+.\n\nI'm not saying it's definitely Alice or Diana, but I am NOT the kill. Voting me loses you the only person giving real timing info. I'd look hardest at Alice's Storage\u2192Medbay window."}}
{"timestamp": 1779381231.702395, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 19, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "Bob, I get the argument, but your defense still doesn\u2019t solve the main issue: your own route is the only one that overlaps both kill spots at relevant times.\n\nFor Charlie, if you really saw him alive in Medbay at tick 13, then the killer had to be in/near Medbay after that \u2014 and you were literally there then. None of Alice, Diana, or I have routes that naturally put us in Medbay after that point.\n\nFor Eve, you were in Security early with her, then you say you came back through Security later and didn\u2019t see the body. But that also means you had another chance to be there right before Diana found it. Diana self-report is possible, sure, but combined with Charlie, your path fits both deaths way more than anyone else\u2019s.\n\nAlice and Diana at least line up with each other for part of the round, and Diana saw me in Medbay early, which matches my route. I still think Bob is the strongest vote here."}}
